  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Ghosts** (1 review): Ghosts appears in the archive for the first time here and is a top ten song [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Night of the Mules**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Ghosts**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **The Irony Engine (Franklin Bruno cover)**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Are You Cleaning Off the Stone?**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **The Bad Doctor**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg1996-03-23.aud.128mp3** (recommended): audience recording; 9 songs; 27 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Audio quality is ideal for the era, sounding just like one of his cassettes [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Crowd was loud enough to feel their presence but never drowned out John [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg1996-03-23.aud.128mp3**: This is a partial show from the Butter archives, missing the first half [1]",
